## Today

::::: columns
::: {.column width="46%"}
**One lesson:** SQL basics on an OMOP CDM extract (`person`, `visit_occurrence`, `condition_occurrence`, `drug_exposure`, `measurement`, `concept`)

**Same data, same queries**, built three different ways

We will compare

- how each one **runs** your code
- how it handles **interactivity**
- how you **share** it
:::

::: {.column width="54%"}
::: small
| Workflow | File | Open it |
|------------------|------------------|------------------|
| **Jupyter** | `sql-basics-jupyter.ipynb` | [notebook](sql-basics-jupyter.ipynb) · [Colab](https://colab.research.google.com/github/{{< meta repo-path >}}/sql-basics-jupyter.ipynb) |
